From: Mozilla.ai <noreply@mozilla.ai>
Date: 2026-05-26
Subject: [PATCH] model: use common_sampler and wire chat-template grammar

agent.cpp's Model uses raw llama_sampler_chain, which can't take a
grammar. Without grammar constraints the model can emit malformed tool
calls that the post-hoc PEG parser then fails to extract. Switch to
common_sampler (the grammar-aware wrapper) and re-initialize it per
generate() call when the chat template supplies a tool-calling grammar.

This mirrors llama-server's wiring at
llama.cpp/tools/server/server-task.cpp:379-476.

After this patch, granite-4.0-micro and Qwen3.5-9B emit syntactically
valid tool calls on the first try (no empty-args misfire), and
common_chat_parse populates parsed_msg.tool_calls without falling back
to the heuristic <tool_call>{json} extractor from patch 0001.
